MCP (Anthropic, 2024-25 open standard, now ~2000 servers) standardizes tool wiring:
- **Transport**: `stdio` (local subprocess) or `SSE`/`Streamable HTTP` (remote). Server is JSON-RPC.
- **Primitives**: `tools` (model-invoked functions with JSON Schema), `resources` (read-only context like files/DB rows), `prompts` (templated system prompts).
- **Lifecycle**: `initialize` -> `tools/list` -> `tools/call` -> `resources/read`. Host mediates permissions; server never auto-executes.

| Primitive | Who calls | Example | Schema |
|---|---|---|---|
| Tool | model via `tools/call` | `github.create_issue` | `inputSchema` JSON Schema |
| Resource | client `resources/read` | `file://repo/README.md` | URI + mime |
| Prompt | client `prompts/get` | `review_pr` template | args -> messages |
| Sampling | server asks host | server needs LLM | host approves |

**Interview Tip:** 'I would sketch host->client->server and say we built an MCP server for our Postgres — tools were read-only `query` with RLS, write tools required human approval, and we versioned tool schemas in CI.'

```typescript
// MCP server (TypeScript SDK) — minimal tool server
import { Server } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/index.js';
import { StdioServerTransport } from '@modelcontextprotocol/sdk/server/stdio.js';
import { z } from 'zod';

const server = new Server({ name: 'my-db', version: '1.0.0' }, { capabilities: { tools: {} } });

server.setRequestHandler({ method: 'tools/list' } as any, async () => ({
  tools: [{
    name: 'db_query',
    description: 'Read-only SQL (SELECT only) on analytics DB',
    inputSchema: { type: 'object', properties: { sql: { type: 'string' }, params: { type: 'array' } }, required: ['sql'] }
  }]
}));

server.setRequestHandler({ method: 'tools/call' } as any, async (req: any) => {
  if (req.params.name === 'db_query') {
    if (!req.params.arguments.sql.trim().toLowerCase().startsWith('select')) throw new Error('only SELECT allowed');
    const rows = await db.query(req.params.arguments.sql, req.params.arguments.params);
    return { content: [{ type: 'text', text: JSON.stringify(rows.slice(0, 50)) }] };
  }
  throw new Error('unknown tool');
});

await server.connect(new StdioServerTransport());
```

