AI SDK 5 (mid-2025, stable) unified streaming:
- **Server**: `streamText({ model, messages, tools, system })` -> `result.toUIMessageStreamResponse()` (or `toDataStreamResponse` legacy). Handles tool calls, `onFinish`, `onStepFinish`, abort via `signal`.
- **Client**: `useChat({ transport: DefaultChatTransport({ api: '/api/chat' }) })` gives `{ messages, sendMessage, status, stop, error }`. Renders `message.parts` (text/tool/state).
- **Protocol**: `UIMessage` stream parts `text-start/delta/end`, `tool-input-start/delta/available`, `error` — not raw OpenAI SSE, so client need not parse provider specifics.

| API | Where | Streams | Key prop |
|---|---|---|---|
| `streamText` | server | text + tool calls | `toUIMessageStreamResponse()` |
| `generateText` | server | none (full) | needs `stream: false` |
| `useChat` | client | incremental `messages` | `transport` + `id` |
| `useCompletion` | client | single text | for autocomplete |

