Layered, not single model:
1) **Input**: regex/PII detector (Presidio), prompt-injection classifier (e.g., `protectai/deberta-v3-prompt-injection`), allowed-intent classifier — block or sanitize before LLM.
2) **LLM hardening**: system prompt with `role` boundaries, tool allowlists, `tool_choice` constraints, and "do not reveal system".
3) **Output**: toxicity (Llama Guard 3 / OpenAI moderation), grounding (Ragas faithfulness or NLI check), JSON schema validation (Zod), and URL/claim allowlist.
4) **Policy on failure**: redact > refuse > escalate. Log guardrail triggers for eval gap.

| Layer | Deterministic | Model-based | Fail mode |
|---|---|---|---|
| PII scrub | regex + Presidio | — | redact inline |
| Prompt injection | heuristic | DeBERTa classifier | block + audit |
| Toxicity / jailbreak | — | Llama Guard 3 | refuse with safe completion |
| Grounding | — | NLI / faithfulness | 'I lack sources' |
| Schema | Zod/JSON Schema | — | repair + re-ask |

**Interview Tip:** 'I would draw input->LLM->output chain and say guardrails are code + small classifiers first, LLM judge second — never rely on the base model alone to police itself.'

```typescript
// Guardrail middleware (pseudo)
import { moderate } from './llamaGuard';
import { detectInjection } from './injectionCheck';
import { z } from 'zod';

const schema = z.object({ answer: z.string(), citations: z.array(z.string()) });

export async function guardedGenerate(prompt: string) {
  if (await detectInjection(prompt)) throw new Error('injection_blocked');
  const raw = await generateText({ model: openai('gpt-4o-mini'), prompt });
  const mod = await moderate(raw.text);
  if (mod.flagged) return { text: 'I can’t help with that.', flagged: true };
  const parsed = schema.safeParse(JSON.parse(raw.text));
  if (!parsed.success) return await repair(raw.text, parsed.error);
  return parsed.data;
}
```

