Agents loop until done — without caps they burn money or spam APIs. Pattern 2025:
- **Hard caps**: `maxSteps`, `maxCost`, `maxDuration` checked before each LLM turn; return `budget_exceeded` with partial trace.
- **Tiered actions**: T0 read-only auto; T1 local write (draft) auto; T2 external (send email, push branch) needs user confirm with preview; T3 irreversible (pay, delete) needs re-auth.
- **Circuit breaker**: 3 consecutive tool errors or same action repeated -> break, summarize failure, ask user.
- **Observability**: every step OTEL span, accumulated tokens visible in UI progress bar.

| Tier | Example | Approval | Timeout |
|---|---|---|---|
| T0 read | search, read file | none | 5s per tool |
| T1 local write | draft doc, create branch | none (sandbox) | 10s |
| T2 external | send email, post comment | click confirm | 30s + user |
| T3 critical | payment, prod deploy | re-auth + type name | block until explicit |

